    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed dataset for a GWAS cohort of 14,894 samples and 5,795,421 variants, including per-chromosome file sizing.",
    "rationale": "The .bed binary format packs 2 bits per sample per variant, so total size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome files follow the same rule for each chromosome's variant count. The largest chromosome carries 632,493 variants (consistent with human chr 1 on a dense imputation panel). The number of per-chromosome files assumes a standard human genome build with 22 autosomes + X + Y + MT = 25 chromosomes.",
